WEBVTT

00:00:19.056 --> 00:00:20.884
Hiya, Harry.

00:00:20.884 --> 00:00:23.060
Ron...

00:00:23.060 --> 00:00:24.452
Fred. George.

00:00:24.452 --> 00:00:26.411
What are you all doing here?

00:00:26.411 --> 00:00:27.978
Rescuing you, of course.

00:00:27.978 --> 00:00:30.458
Now, come on.
Get your trunk.

00:00:35.899 --> 00:00:37.640
You'd better stand back.

00:00:38.902 --> 00:00:41.426
Let's go.

00:00:45.386 --> 00:00:48.085
What was it?

00:00:50.696 --> 00:00:52.611
UNCLE VERNON:
Potter!

00:00:52.611 --> 00:00:54.439
Dad! What's going on?

00:00:57.268 --> 00:00:58.748
Go! Go! Go!

00:00:58.748 --> 00:00:59.836
Dad, hurry up!

00:01:01.098 --> 00:01:02.621
Come on!

00:01:02.621 --> 00:01:03.970
Come on, Harry!
Hurry up!

00:01:05.319 --> 00:01:08.105
Petunia, he's escaping!

00:01:08.105 --> 00:01:10.542
RON: I've got you, Harry.

00:01:10.542 --> 00:01:11.543
Come here!

00:01:11.543 --> 00:01:12.892
Let go of me!

00:01:12.892 --> 00:01:14.590
Oh, no, boy.

00:01:14.590 --> 00:01:16.983
You and that bloody pigeon
aren't going anywhere!

00:01:16.983 --> 00:01:19.246
Get off!Drive!

00:01:21.118 --> 00:01:22.510
[UNCLE VERNON SCREAMS]

00:01:26.906 --> 00:01:28.734
Dad!

00:01:42.835 --> 00:01:46.230
By the way, Harry,
happy birthday.

00:02:13.387 --> 00:02:14.824
[WHISPERS]
Come on.

00:02:17.827 --> 00:02:20.351
Okay, come on, shh!

00:02:20.351 --> 00:02:23.223
Okay, come on!

00:02:30.056 --> 00:02:33.233
Do you think it'd be all right
if we had some of this?

00:02:33.233 --> 00:02:34.495
Yeah, Mum
will never know.

00:02:51.730 --> 00:02:54.907
It's not much,
but it's home.

00:02:54.907 --> 00:02:58.519
I think it's brilliant.

00:02:58.519 --> 00:03:02.480
Where have you been?

00:03:02.480 --> 00:03:05.265
Harry, how wonderful
to see you, dear.

00:03:05.265 --> 00:03:08.181
Beds empty! No note!

00:03:08.181 --> 00:03:09.661
Car gone!

00:03:09.661 --> 00:03:12.882
You could have died!
You could have been seen!

00:03:12.882 --> 00:03:15.319
Of course,
I don't blame you, Harry, dear.

00:03:15.319 --> 00:03:19.279
They were starving him, Mum.
There were bars on his window.

00:03:19.279 --> 00:03:22.892
Well, you'd best hope
I don't put bars on your window,

00:03:22.892 --> 00:03:24.284
Ronald Weasley.

00:03:24.284 --> 00:03:26.504
Come on, Harry,
time for a spot of breakfast.

00:03:26.504 --> 00:03:28.245
Here we are, Harry.

00:03:28.245 --> 00:03:30.073
Now tuck in.

00:03:30.073 --> 00:03:31.944
That's it.

00:03:31.944 --> 00:03:33.816
There we go.

00:03:33.816 --> 00:03:36.427
Mummy,
have you seen my jumper?

00:03:36.427 --> 00:03:38.124
Yes, dear,
it was on the cat.

00:03:38.124 --> 00:03:39.299
Hello.

00:03:44.261 --> 00:03:45.784
Wh-what did I do?

00:03:45.784 --> 00:03:47.046
Ginny...

00:03:47.046 --> 00:03:48.744
she's been talking
about you all summer.

00:03:48.744 --> 00:03:50.354
A bit annoying, really.

00:03:50.354 --> 00:03:52.399
Morning, Weasleys.

00:03:52.399 --> 00:03:53.705
Morning, Dad.
Morning, Dad.

00:03:53.705 --> 00:03:56.969
What a night!
Nine raids. Nine!

00:03:56.969 --> 00:03:58.405
Raids?

00:03:58.405 --> 00:04:00.016
Dad works
in the Ministry of Magic,

00:04:00.016 --> 00:04:02.453
in the Misuse
of Muggle Artifacts Office.

00:04:02.453 --> 00:04:03.802
Dad loves Muggles.

00:04:03.802 --> 00:04:05.804
Thinks
they're fascinating.

00:04:05.804 --> 00:04:08.241
Well, now...
Ah.

00:04:09.677 --> 00:04:11.505
And who are you?

00:04:11.505 --> 00:04:13.116
Oh, sorry, sir.

00:04:13.116 --> 00:04:15.814
I'm Harry, sir.
Harry Potter.

00:04:15.814 --> 00:04:18.991
Good lord.
Are you really?

00:04:20.732 --> 00:04:22.647
Well, Ron's told us
all about you, of course.

00:04:22.647 --> 00:04:24.170
When did he get here?

00:04:24.170 --> 00:04:25.737
This morning.

00:04:25.737 --> 00:04:29.001
Your sons flew
that enchanted car of yours

00:04:29.001 --> 00:04:31.090
to Surrey and back last night.

00:04:31.090 --> 00:04:32.483
Did you really?

00:04:32.483 --> 00:04:34.702
How'd it go?BOYS: Oh, it was--

00:04:34.702 --> 00:04:38.184
I mean...that was
very wrong, indeed, boys.

00:04:38.184 --> 00:04:39.577
Very wrong of you.

00:04:41.231 --> 00:04:44.887
Now, Harry, you must know
all about Muggles.

00:04:44.887 --> 00:04:46.453
Tell me...

00:04:46.453 --> 00:04:49.152
what exactly is the function
of a rubber duck?

00:04:49.152 --> 00:04:51.719
Oh, um...

00:04:53.591 --> 00:04:55.114
Oh, that'll be Errol
with the post.

00:04:55.114 --> 00:04:57.116
[♪♪♪]

00:05:00.380 --> 00:05:01.817
[BOYS GROAN]

00:05:01.817 --> 00:05:03.906
Oh, fetch it, will you,
Percy, please?

00:05:05.385 --> 00:05:08.301
RON: He's always doing that.

00:05:09.912 --> 00:05:12.044
Oh, look,
it's our Hogwarts letters.

00:05:12.044 --> 00:05:14.003
And they've sent us
Harry's as well.

00:05:14.003 --> 00:05:15.918
Dumbledore must know
you're here, Harry.

00:05:15.918 --> 00:05:17.441
Doesn't miss a trick, that man.

00:05:17.441 --> 00:05:19.530
This lot won't come cheap, Mum.

00:05:19.530 --> 00:05:22.402
These spell books alone
are very expensive.

00:05:22.402 --> 00:05:24.056
We'll manage.

00:05:24.056 --> 00:05:27.494
There's only one place
we're going to get all of this:

00:05:27.494 --> 00:05:28.974
Diagon Alley.

00:05:30.019 --> 00:05:31.150
Right...

00:05:31.150 --> 00:05:32.282
Here we are, Harry.

00:05:32.282 --> 00:05:34.066
You go first, dear.

00:05:34.066 --> 00:05:36.416
But Harry's never traveled
by Floo powder before, Mum.

00:05:36.416 --> 00:05:37.940
Floo powder?

00:05:37.940 --> 00:05:39.158
Well, you
go first, Ron,

00:05:39.158 --> 00:05:40.551
so Harry can see
how it's done.

00:05:40.551 --> 00:05:42.901
Yes.

00:05:42.901 --> 00:05:44.772
In you go.

00:05:44.772 --> 00:05:46.383
That's it.

00:05:50.604 --> 00:05:52.432
Diagon Alley!

00:05:58.047 --> 00:05:59.439
You see?

00:05:59.439 --> 00:06:01.180
It's quite easy, dear.
Don't be afraid.

00:06:01.180 --> 00:06:03.617
Come on.

00:06:03.617 --> 00:06:05.010
Come on.

00:06:05.010 --> 00:06:06.098
In you go.

00:06:06.098 --> 00:06:07.970
That's it. Mind your head.

00:06:07.970 --> 00:06:09.841
That's right.

00:06:09.841 --> 00:06:11.887
Now, take your Floo powder.

00:06:13.845 --> 00:06:16.369
That's it, very good.

00:06:16.369 --> 00:06:17.588
Now, don't forget to speak

00:06:17.588 --> 00:06:20.721
very, very clearly.

00:06:21.897 --> 00:06:25.030
Diagonally.

00:06:30.644 --> 00:06:32.037
What did he say, dear?

00:06:32.037 --> 00:06:33.386
"Diagonally."

00:06:33.386 --> 00:06:34.735
I thought he did.

